## The affected product

The floor normalizes the filer's vendor and product strings and matches them to the CPE dictionary,
exactly and then by a token set ratio; the retrieval ranks every CPE vendor and product by cosine to
the CVE's joined text. A CVE is offered only the names the NVD had created by its day 0.

{% if has("models.product.floor.threshold") %}
The floor's threshold is chosen by the F1 of each CVE's first candidate on development (DECISIONS.md,
the change request on the product floor's threshold), and it is {{ v("models.product.floor.threshold") }}.
On the {{ v("models.product.dev_cves") }} development CVEs with a labeled product, the share of their
labeled pairs found in the first ten candidates is {{ v("models.product.floor.dev_recall_at_10") }} for
the floor without its threshold, {{ v("models.product.floor_at_threshold.dev_recall_at_10") }} with it,
and {{ v("models.product.retrieval.dev_recall_at_10") }} for the retrieval.
{% endif %}

## Calibration and conformal sets

Each fill head is scaled by one temperature fit on development by negative log likelihood, and the
exploitation score is mapped by an isotonic regression fit on development. The calibration error is
taken over equal width bins of the top label probability, with a bootstrap interval. Split conformal
sets with adaptive sets are fit on development at a target coverage of {{ plan.conformal.target_coverage }},
and their coverage is measured on test, overall and by filer type, because test is later
than development and the coverage a set promises holds only for rows like the ones it was fit on.

{% if has("models.calibration.band_temperature") %}
The band's temperature is {{ v("models.calibration.band_temperature") }}; its development calibration
error is {{ v("models.calibration.band_dev_ece_before") }} before scaling and
{{ v("models.calibration.band_dev_ece_after") }} after.
{% endif %}

## The CVEs the NVD skipped

The NVD's analyzed CVEs after April 2026 are a selected sample, so a score on them says little
about the CVEs it skipped. The shadow CVEs it did analyze are weighted by the odds that a CVE like
them was skipped, from the Phase 1 domain classifier fit out of half, clipped at
{{ plan.reweighting.clip }}, and the band kappa is shown plain and weighted, with Kish's effective
sample size, never one without the other.

{% if has("models.reweighting.fallback.plain_qwk") %}
For the primary model the plain kappa is {{ v("models.reweighting.fallback.plain_qwk") }} and the
weighted one {{ v("models.reweighting.fallback.weighted_qwk") }}, on an effective sample of
{{ v("models.reweighting.fallback.ess") }}.
{% endif %}

